<title>USA: CBOT re-appoints two non-member directors.</title>
<headline>CBOT re-appoints two non-member directors.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board of Trade board late Tuesday re-appointed two non-member directors to four-year terms on its 27-person board.</p>
<p>The board at its regular meeting re-appointed Robert Hamada, finance professor and dean of the University of Chicago Graduate School of Business; and Robert Michel, senior advisor, corporate and legal affairs, Hogan &amp; Hartson.</p>
<p>Their terms expire Dec 31, 2000, according to a CBOT board meeting bulletin.</p>
<p>CBOT members held their annual election on December 11. ((DerivativesDesk(312)408-8750/E-mail:derivatives@reuters.com))</p>
